# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
C('afval', "one plain park path seen from the side with a flat ground line, one plain litter bin with an open top at the right, one crumpled paper ball, one adult in plain clothes, same distance from the viewer, a plain tree behind. Only whether the ball goes into the bin or comes up from the ground changes.",
  "Ik gooi het papier weg en mijn zus raapt het papier op.", "I throw the paper away and my sister picks the paper up.")
K('weggooien', "One drawing, one panel. An adult stands beside a litter bin with one arm swung back and the crumpled paper ball just leaving the hand towards the bin's open top, a curved dotted path from the hand to the bin. The ground is clean.",
  "a crumpled ball on a dotted arc towards the bin's open top.",
  "an adult bending to pick the ball from the ground (oprapen); an adult handing a ball to a child (doorgeven); an adult tossing a ball into the air to play (not the card); an adult pushing a bin along the path (not the card).",
  "Pair with oprapen. The only difference is the direction: the ball flies towards the bin here, rises from the ground into a hand there.",
  "gooi ... weg", "Ik gooi het papier weg.", "I throw away the paper.", "heeft weggegooid",
  "Een volwassene zwaait de arm naar achteren en een prop papier vliegt in een boog naar een prullenbak.")
K('oprapen', "One drawing, one panel. An adult bends at the waist beside the same bin and picks a crumpled paper ball up off the ground with one hand, the other hand on the knee, the ball a hand's width above the ground and the bin still empty beside them.",
  "a bent adult lifting a crumpled ball off the ground.",
  "the ball flying towards the bin from a swung arm (weggooien); an adult lifting a heavy box with both hands (optillen); an adult picking apples from a tree (not the card); an adult sweeping the path with a broom (schoonmaken).",
  "Pair with weggooien. The only difference is the direction: the ball is lifted off the ground here, thrown towards the bin there.",
  "raap ... op", "Ik raap het papier op.", "I pick up the paper.", "heeft opgeraapt",
  "Een gebogen volwassene pakt met één hand een prop papier van de grond.")

C('doos', "one plain cardboard box with two flap lines on top seen side-on, one adult in plain clothes whole-figure, a flat floor line, same size on the page, a plain wall behind. Only whether the box is lifted off the floor or set down on a table changes.",
  "Ik til de doos op en zet hem daarna op tafel neer.", "I lift the box up and then put it down on the table.")
K('optillen', "One drawing, one panel. An adult with bent knees and a straight back lifts a plain cardboard box clear of the floor with both hands under it, the box a hand's width above the floor and the knees still bent, a small arrow pointing upward. A plain table stands empty beside them.",
  "a box a hand's width above the floor with bent knees and an upward arrow.",
  "the box standing flat on the table with the hands letting go (neerzetten); an adult pushing a box along the floor (not the card); an adult carrying the box through a doorway (meenemen); an adult picking up a ball (oprapen).",
  "Pair with neerzetten. The only difference is the box: a hand's width above the floor here, standing flat on the table there.",
  "til ... op", "Ik til de doos op.", "I lift up the box.", "heeft opgetild",
  "Een volwassene met gebogen knieën houdt een doos met beide handen een stuk boven de vloer.")
K('neerzetten', "One drawing, one panel. An adult stands upright beside a plain table and lowers the same cardboard box until its base just meets the table top, both hands still under the box and the arms at a slight bend. A small downward arrow sits above the box.",
  "a box base just touching the table with hands still under it.",
  "the box lifted off the floor by an adult with bent knees (optillen); a glass lowered onto a table (not the card); a box dropped from height with a crash burst (not the card); a box left on a doorstep (achterlaten).",
  "Pair with optillen. The only difference is the box: its base meeting the table here, a hand's width above the floor there.",
  "zet ... neer", "Ik zet de doos op tafel neer.", "I put the box down on the table.", "heeft neergezet",
  "Een volwassene laat een doos met beide handen zakken tot hij op een tafel staat.")

C('boot', "one plain small rowing boat seen side-on on a pond or lake, open water behind, beside a plain wooden post on a grassy bank, a rope in plain loops, same distance from the viewer, a flat water line. Only whether the rope is tied round the post or hangs free in the water changes.",
  "Ik bind de boot vast en later bind ik hem weer los.", "I tie up the boat and later I untie it again.")
K('vastbinden', "One drawing, one panel. An adult kneels on the bank and pulls the boat's rope tight round a wooden post with a final knot, the rope straight and taut between the post and the boat's front. The boat sits snug against the bank.",
  "a taut rope knotted round the post and held by the adult's hands.",
  "the rope hanging slack off the post (losbinden); an adult tying a shoelace (not the card); an adult locking a door with a key (afsluiten); an adult fastening a belt (not the card).",
  "Pair with losbinden. The only difference is the rope: knotted tight round the post here, hanging free of it there.",
  "bind ... vast", "Ik bind de boot vast.", "I tie up the boat.", "heeft vastgebonden",
  "Een volwassene trekt een touw met een knoop strak om een paal en de boot ligt tegen de kant.")
K('losbinden', "One drawing, one panel. An adult kneels on the bank and lifts a loop of rope off the wooden post with one hand, the rope slack and hanging in a curve, the boat drifting a short distance from the bank with a small arrow pointing away.",
  "a slack rope loop lifted off the post with the boat drifting away.",
  "the rope pulled taut round the post (vastbinden); a boat sailing alone across open water (not the card); a rope coiled on the ground (not the card); an adult cutting a rope with scissors (not the card).",
  "Pair with vastbinden. The only difference is the rope: slack and lifted off the post here, taut and knotted round it there.",
  "bind ... los", "Ik bind de boot los.", "I untie the boat.", "heeft losgebonden",
  "Een volwassene haalt een lus touw van een paal terwijl de boot langzaam van de kant afdrijft.")

C('blik', "two adults seen from the shoulders up, side by side on a plain bench in profile, same distance from the viewer, a plain wall behind. Only whether the second adult's face turns towards the first with eyes open wide, or turns the other way changes.",
  "Ik kijk mijn buurman aan, maar hij kijkt weg.", "I look at my neighbour, but he looks away.")
K('aankijken', "One drawing, one panel. Two adults sit side by side on a bench, and the nearer one turns the whole head to face the other, eyes open wide, with a short dotted line from the eyes to the other person's eyes. The second adult faces forward.",
  "a turned head with a dotted line from the eyes to the other person's eyes.",
  "the head turned away from the other person (wegkijken); both adults staring forward with no turn of the head (not the card); an adult looking through a window (not the card); an adult squinting at a map (not the card).",
  "Pair with wegkijken. The only difference is the head: turned towards the other person with a dotted line here, turned away from them there.",
  "kijk ... aan", "Ik kijk mijn buurman aan.", "I look at my neighbour.", "heeft aangekeken",
  "Twee volwassenen zitten op een bankje en één draait het hoofd naar de ander met wijd open ogen.")
K('wegkijken', "One drawing, one panel. Two adults sit side by side on the same bench, and the nearer one turns the whole head the other way, the chin pointing to the far edge of the picture, eyes cast away, a dotted line from the eyes towards the edge. The second adult faces forward.",
  "a head turned away with a dotted line from the eyes towards the edge.",
  "the head turned towards the other person with a dotted line (aankijken); an adult closing both eyes (not the card); an adult looking at a watch (not the card); an adult ducking behind a newspaper (not the card).",
  "Pair with aankijken. The only difference is the head: turned away with a dotted line to the edge here, turned towards the other person there.",
  "kijk ... weg", "Ik kijk snel weg.", "I quickly look away.", "heeft weggekeken",
  "Twee volwassenen zitten op een bankje en één draait het gezicht naar de andere kant.")
